app/admin/page.tsx, abandoned-checkouts, gift-cards, and walkin all called
a requireAdmin()-gated data fetch unconditionally at the top of the page
render. requireAdmin() throws instead of returning false for a logged-out
or unauthorized visitor, and nothing caught that throw — so instead of
redirecting to /admin/login, the whole page crashed with Next.js's generic
"Application error: a server-side exception has occurred" screen.

Root cause of why this could be hit at all: middleware only checks the
legacy admin_auth cookie before letting a request through to these pages;
it doesn't validate per-tenant Supabase-session admin status the way
lib/auth-guard.ts's real check does. A stale/mismatched admin_auth cookie
(e.g. from a different tenant, per auth-guard's Orlando-only legacy path)
gets past middleware but then fails requireAdmin() inside the page render.

Fix: call the non-throwing isAdminForCurrentLocation() check first on each
of these four pages and redirect to /admin/login on failure, before any
admin-gated action runs. Same pattern already used by
app/operator/owner-login/page.tsx and the fix already applied to
syncFacilityStripeStatus's public call site in
app/actions/facility-payments.ts.

Audited every app/admin/**/page.tsx for this same unconditional-call
pattern; these were the only three beyond the already-fixed hub page.
